UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Cable Corp., operating as Custom Wire & Cable, is headquartered in Westbury, New York. The company was founded in 1974 as a small Long Island distributor and has since grown into a global supplier of industrial wire and cable.

The company maintains an inventory of more than 15,000 active wire and cable variations, ranging from high-temperature wire and coaxial cable to multi-conductor and fiber optic products. Beyond distribution, Custom Cable provides value-added fabrication services including precision striping, twisting, paralleling, bundling, custom printing, dyeing, lashing, and the assembly of generator cable assemblies and fiber patch cords. Its capabilities also cover custom cable solutions, technical consulting, and quality compliance testing to standards such as UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, and VW-1.

Custom Cable serves manufacturers, contractors, OEMs, and distributors across a range of industries. Testimonials cite customers in manufacturing, aerospace, construction, electronics, and energy & utilities sectors. The company’s products and services support applications in factories, hospitals, data centers, and transportation systems worldwide.

The firm emphasizes a specification-driven approach rather than selling by description, highlighting its technical expertise, responsive service, and dependable turnaround times. Its team averages over 25 years of experience per sales professional, and the company positions its long-term customer relationships and rapid fulfillment — including emergency shipments and just-in-time programs — as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision color striping", "Custom wire twisting", "Paralleling", "Bundling and securing", "Bundling with custom printing", "Cable dyeing", "Lashing", "Generator cable assembly", "Fiber patch cord assembly", "Custom cable solutions (non-standard configurations)", "Inventory management and rapid fulfillment", "Technical support and consulting", "Quality and standards compliance (UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, VW-1)"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Aerospace", "Construction", "Electronics", "Energy & Utilities"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Copper", "Fiber optic", "High-temperature insulation", "Plenum-rated materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["15,000+ active wire and cable variations in stock", "Sales team averages over 25 years of experience", "Paralleling service reduces labor costs by 50\u201370%", "Custom generator cable assemblies and fiber patch cords built to order", "Materials tested to UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, and VW-1 standards"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Westbury, New York -> db", "15,000+ active wire and cable variations in stock -> /capabilities", "Sales professionals average over 25 years experience -> /capabilities", "Paralleling reduces labor costs 50-70% -> /capabilities", "Capabilities: striping, twisting, paralleling, bundling, custom printing, dyeing, lashing, generator cable assemblies, fiber patch cords -> /capabilities", "Industries served: manufacturing, aerospace, construction, electronics, energy & utilities -> / (testimonials)", "Customer types: manufacturers, contractors, OEMs, distributors -> /about-us", "Standards compliance: UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, VW-1 -> /capabilities", "RoHS certification -> db", "Custom cable assemblies and fiber patch cords built to order -> /capabilities", "Specification-driven approach, not selling by description -> /about-us", "Rapid fulfillment: emergency shipments, just-in-time programs -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Cable has been a single-source supplier for electrical and electronic wire and cable. In addition to maintaining one of the industry''s most extensive inventories, we provide value-added services, custom fabrication, and responsive logistics.", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-cable-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Cut & Fab operates from Mandan, North Dakota, where its staff has been active in metal fabrication since 1992. The company began with a focus on HVAC fabrication and general construction trade work, building experience in evaluating drawings and resolving design issues before production.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication services, including HVAC fittings, galvanized and stainless steel components, copper countertops, and one-off special projects. Its equipment includes a 6‑by‑12‑foot waterjet capable of cutting materials up to seven inches thick and as thin as .002 inch, handling stone, marble, granite, plastics, foam, wood, and ceramics. A 5‑by‑10‑foot plasma table cuts metal up to 3/16 inch, primarily for HVAC ductwork and metal‑art pieces. The company can act as a subcontractor for large jobs or manage a project from initial design through final delivery.

Customers come from the HVAC, general construction, and metal‑arts sectors. Contractors seek the firm for ductwork and fitting fabrication, while designers and artists use its waterjet for decorative pieces in stone, metal, and other media. The company also serves clients needing custom countertops and miscellaneous fabricated assemblies.

The firm emphasizes its ability to review customer drawings, identify potential problems, and suggest work‑arounds, a capability developed over decades of trade experience. It also offers turnkey project packages that cover the full fabrication cycle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HVAC fabrication", "Custom metal fabrication", "Waterjet cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Drawing evaluation and feasibility", "Project management", "Subcontracting", "Copper countertop fabrication", "Special project fabrication", "Metal arts design"], "industries": ["HVAC", "General construction", "Metal arts"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Stainless steel", "Copper", "Stone", "Marble", "Granite", "Plastic", "Foam", "Wood", "Ceramics"], "equipment": ["Water Jet (6'' x 12'' table)", "Plasma Table (5'' x 10'')"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Drawing evaluation and feasibility work\u2011arounds", "Waterjet cutting up to 7\u2033 thick and .002\u2033 thin", "Plasma cutting up to 3/16\u2033 for HVAC and metal art", "Turnkey project management from design to delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> db", "Headquarters Mandan, North Dakota -> db", "Staff in business since 1992 specializing in HVAC fabrication -> homepage", "Custom metal fabrication, HVAC fittings, galvanized, stainless steel, copper countertops -> homepage", "Waterjet 6''x12'' cuts up to 7\" thick and .002\" thin, cuts stone, marble, granite, plastic, foam, wood, ceramics -> homepage", "Plasma table 5''x10'' cuts up to 3/16\" metal for HVAC and metal arts -> homepage", "Subcontractor for large projects, turnkey project packages -> homepage", "Industries: HVAC, general construction, metal arts -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom metal fabrication company providing customers with expert assistance in completing their project.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-cut-and-fab' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Metal Fabrication, Inc. was founded in 1979 in Mobile, Alabama, along Dauphin Island Parkway. The company established strategic relationships with U.S. material suppliers to secure competitive raw material pricing, a foundation that continues to shape its cost structure today.

The shop provides industrial and marine metal fabrication services. Industrial work spans carbon steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, covering metal bending, custom fabrication, and projects ranging from prototype designs to facility renovations. Marine fabrication focuses on full-service top-side work for both commercial vessels and pleasure craft, including interior and exterior custom builds in the same three alloys. An in-house engineering team supports projects with CAD-driven design and drafting using AutoCAD, Rhino, Fusion 360, and SOLIDWORKS, offering surface modeling, solid modeling, piping design, and finite element analysis.

Customers come from industrial and marine sectors, including commercial ship operators and recreational boat owners seeking custom topside fabrication.

