s, whether carbon steel, stainless steel or aluminum, CMFI is the industry leader. Our customers depend on us to produce quality products involving both metal bending, as well as custom metal fabrication.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-metal-fabrication-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Port Washington, Wisconsin, Custom Wire Technologies (CWT) has over 50 years of industry experience as an OEM medical component manufacturer. The company specializes in precision wire components for the medical device sector.

CWT produces fine and ultra-fine wire components, including guidewires, coiled components, and Nitinol products. Its capabilities cover wire coiling (reinforcement coils, compression springs, Nitinol coils), wire grinding (core wire, mandrel, hypotube, orthopedic), wire forming (Nitinol shape setting, K-wires), laser welding of ultra-fine wire, laser marking, medical pad printing, and cleanroom assembly. The company handles production runs from prototypes to large contract volumes, offering both bulk non-sterile and single-unit sterile assembly.

The company serves medical device OEMs ranging from large manufacturers to entrepreneurial startups. Its components are used in catheter accessories, cardiovascular valves, guidewires, and a variety of dental and surgical devices. CWT emphasizes manufacturing process validation and works with customers worldwide.

CWT highlights its consistent precision, high-quality repeatability, and implementation of the latest technology as key differentiators. The firm states that its management and production teams deliver unparalleled customer service, quality, and cost-effectiveness for specific medical device needs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire coiling (Nitinol, reinforcement, fine wire, compression springs)", "Coil finishing", "Wire grinding (core wire, mandrel, hypotube, orthopedic)", "Wire forming (Nitinol shape setting, Nitinol K-wires)", "Laser welding (ultra-fine wire)", "Laser marking", "Medical pad printing", "Cleanroom assembly", "Manufacturing process validation", "Custom guidewire development, prototyping, and assembly", "Fine wire welding", "Laser processing", "Custom fine wire design"], "industries": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Catheter accessories", "Cardiovascular valves", "Guidewires", "Dental devices", "Surgical devices"], "materials": ["Nitinol", "Fine wire", "Ultra-fine wire"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to large contract runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 50 years of industry experience", "ISO 13485 certified quality management", "Cleanroom assembly for sterile medical components", "Laser welding of ultra-fine wire with specialty in small diameters", "Production runs from prototype to large contract volumes"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Port Washington, Wisconsin -> / (address) and db", "Over 50 years industry experience -> /about", "ISO 13485 certified -> /about and db", "Manufactures medical guide wires, fine wire components, Nitinol products -> / and description", "Processes: coiling, grinding, wire forming, laser welding, laser marking, pad printing, cleanroom assembly, process validation -> / and /about", "Serves medical device OEMs, catheter accessories, cardiovascular valves, guidewires, dental and surgical devices -> /", "Production runs from prototypes to large contract runs -> description and /", "Laser welding of ultra-fine wire specialty -> / (products list)", "Serves large medical OEM manufacturers to small entrepreneurial medical device startups -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a leading OEM medical component manufacturer", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-wire-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Wood Artistry operates from Peever, South Dakota, where Troy and Sharon Foster founded the family-owned shop after Troy completed his service in the United States Air Force. A disabled veteran, Troy has spent a lifetime working with wood, from home building to custom pieces. The business is a multi-generational enterprise: the Fosters have been married for over 50 years and their six children, fourteen grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren all actively contribute to daily operations.

The company produces handcrafted wooden gifts, decor, and keepsakes entirely in the United States. Its catalog spans snack trays and serving boards, cribbage boards, lidded boxes with magnetic closures, plaques and wall signs, magnets, wood toys, and numismatic displays for coins and medallions. A dedicated wood engraving service adds personalized finishing touches. Products are shaped from a rotating selection of domestic and exotic hardwoods — including Sapele, Yellowheart, Wenge, Bubinga, Paduk, Purpleheart, Zebrawood, Lacewood, and Canary — with attention to grain, finish, and detail.

Customers range from individuals seeking personalized gifts for birthdays, military honors, or corporate thank-yous to restaurants and businesses ordering custom signs. The patriotic and military-themed line — featuring branch-specific lids, eagle boxes, and flag-inspired trays — serves veterans, active-duty families, and collectors. Numismatic trays and boxes cater to coin collectors. Nationwide shipping extends the shop''s reach beyond its rural South Dakota location.

The Fosters frame the business around generational pride and the desire to turn meaningful moments into lasting keepsakes. Troy''s military background is cited as a source of discipline and dedication that informs every build, while the family''s collective involvement ensures each piece carries a personal touch that mass-produced alternatives cannot replicate.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wood engraving", "Custom woodworking", "Handcrafted wood products", "Wood sign making", "Wood turning", "Laser engraving", "Custom wood gifts", "Personalized wood products"], "industries": ["Gift and specialty retail", "Home decor", "Military and veteran memorabilia", "Numismatic and collectible displays", "Restaurant and business signage"], "materials": ["Sapele", "Yellowheart", "Wenge", "Bubinga", "Paduk", "Purpleheart", "Zebrawood", "Lacewood", "Canary", "Maple", "Walnut", "Exotic hardwoods", "Domestic hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-generational family operation with hands-on involvement from children, grandchildren, and great-grandchildren", "Founder Troy Foster is a Disabled Veteran of the U.S. Air Force, bringing military discipline to craftsmanship", "Every piece made in the USA with attention to grain, finish, and detail", "Nationwide shipping on custom wood gifts and keepsakes", "Personalized engraving service for custom finishing touches"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Custom Wood Artistry -> db", "Founders: Troy and Sharon Foster -> /", "Location: Peever, South Dakota -> db, /", "Troy Foster is a Disabled Veteran of the U.S. Air Force -> /", "Family-owned, multi-generational involvement (children, grandchildren, great-grandchildren) -> /", "Married over 50 years, six children, fourteen grandchildren, two great-grandchildren -> /", "Business started after Troy''s military service -> /", "Products: snack trays, cribbage boards, boxes, plaques, magnets, wood toys, patrioti