UPDATE companies SET description='DAD Manufacturing, Inc. is headquartered in Hiawatha, Iowa, with a second high-volume facility in nearby Lisbon. The company was founded in 1980 by Dave Dohrmann, who remains owner and sales manager, and it operates as a family-owned business. From the start, DAD focused on solving a persistent problem in stainless steel fabrication: heat distortion during welding that caused warping and loss of dimensional accuracy. The founders developed proprietary welding processes and fixturing techniques to maintain shape and hold tight tolerances on large weldments.

The company specializes in stainless steel and aluminum fabrication and polishing. Core processes include laser cutting (tube and flat), bending, rolling, machining, TIG/MIG/spot welding, forming, and polishing to 2B cosmetic, #4 sanitary, and #8 aesthetic finishes. Powder coating and mechanical, electrical, or manual assembly are also offered in-house. DAD reports 2,632,781 parts fabricated, 217,348 jobs completed, and a 99% on-time delivery rate across 536 customers served. Its two Iowa plants together provide prototype, pre-production, and high-volume capacity.

DAD serves food manufacturing, pharmaceutical manufacturing, appliance and furniture, wind power, transportation, and government sectors. Long-standing customers include a pharmaceutical equipment manufacturer with a 36-year relationship and an ultrasonic tank manufacturer with a 21-year relationship. Specific projects cited include coating pan tanks for food and pharma, wedge wire baskets for the corn industry, custom aluminum ladders for wind power, and staircase railings for government facilities.

The company emphasizes its innovative welding and fixturing technology that enables statistically repeatable processes and tolerances of ±1 mm on weldments up to 10 feet long and 2,300 pounds. Hand polishing by experienced craftsmen achieves precise surface finishes. DAD attributes its differentiation to high quality, customer service, on-time delivery, consistency, tight tolerances, and family values cultivated over more than four decades.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting (tube and flat)", "Bending", "Rolling", "Machining", "TIG welding", "MIG welding", "Spot welding", "Forming", "Polishing (2B cosmetic, #4 sanitary, #8 aesthetic)", "Powder coating", "Mechanical assembly", "Electrical assembly", "Manual assembly", "Fixturing design and build"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Pharmaceutical manufacturing", "Appliance and furniture", "Wind power", "Transportation", "Government", "Agricultural (corn processing)"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype, pre-production, or high-volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b11 mm on weldments up to 10 ft long and 2,300 lbs", "built_on": ["Proprietary welding processes that prevent warping and hold \u00b11 mm tolerances on large weldments", "Hand polishing to #4 sanitary and #8 aesthetic finishes with certified RA values", "Fixturing technology for statistically repeatable production", "99% on-time delivery across 536 customers", "Family-owned continuity with 40+ year customer relationships"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Hiawatha, Iowa; second plant in Lisbon, Iowa -> homepage", "Founded 1980 by Dave Dohrmann; family-owned -> homepage", "Proprietary welding processes to prevent warping and hold tight tolerances -> homepage", "Processes: laser cutting, bending, rolling, machining, TIG/MIG/spot welding, forming, polishing, powder coating, assembly -> homepage", "Scale: 2,632,781 parts fabricated, 217,348 jobs, 99% on-time, 536 customers -> homepage", "Industries: food, pharma, appliance/furniture, wind power, transportation, government -> homepage", "Customer examples: pharmaceutical equipment manufacturer (36-year), ultrasonic tank manufacturer (21-year) -> homepage", "Tolerances: \u00b11 mm on weldments up to 10 ft, 2,300 lbs -> homepage", "Certification: ISO 9001:2015 -> homepage", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, copper -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We use your custom 3D metal designs and our fabrication and polishing capabilities to serve any industry and make any product.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dad-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DEM Medical, based in Painesville, Ohio, operates as an FDA-registered contract manufacturer of Class I and Class II medical devices. The company was formed through the consolidation of Virtec Medical and Virtec Enterprises, bringing together domestic design, injection molding, electronics, and assembly under a single quality system.

The firm provides end-to-end medical device development, from concept creation and benchmarking through prototyping, validation, and conversion to high-volume production. Its in-house capabilities include additive manufacturing, precision machining, injection molding, printed circuit board assembly, custom cabling, and tooling design and fabrication. The company supports programs ranging from early-stage prototypes to medium-volume runs and full-scale production.

DEM Medical serves medical OEMs, startups, and pilot programs across a range of device categories. Past applications include homecare dialysis and monitoring systems, heated humidifiers, gastric calibration tubes, surgical tables, suction devices, laparoscopic surgical instruments, catheters, ventilatory devices, and laser therapy equipment. The company also supports diagnostic and monitoring equipment, surgical devices, and wearable or instrument-integrated designs.

The company emphasizes a vertically integrated, U.S.-based model that keeps engineering, tooling, molding, and assembly within one ISO 13485:2016-certified quality system. This approach is intended to protect schedule and compliance during design transfer, offering customers a single accountable partner rather than a fragmented vendor chain. DEM Medical also provides FDA 510(k) documentation support and maintains traceable design history files.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered (Class I and II)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Cabling & Connectors", "Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Analog & Digital Communication", "Tooling Design & Fabrication", "3D Printing & Prototyping", "Injection Molded Components", "Additive Manufacturing", "Precision Machining", "Medical Device Assembly", "Design Transfer", "FDA 510(k) Documentation Support", "Design History File Management", "Medical Device Prototyping", "Medical Device Validation", "Regulatory Compliance Support"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Class I Medical Devices", "Class II Medical Devices", "Homecare Dialysis and Monitoring", "Heated Humidifiers", "Gastric Calibration Tubes", "Surgical Tables", "Suction Devices", "Laparoscopic Surgical Devices", "Catheters", "Ventilatory Devices", "Laser Therapy", "Diagnostic Devices", "Monitoring Equipment", "Surgical Devices", "Wearable Medical Devices", "Instrument-Integrated Designs"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3D Printers", "Injection Molding Machines", "CNC Machining Centers", "PCB Assembly Equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated in-house engineering, tooling, molding, and assembly under one quality system", "U.S.-based manufacturing with ISO 13485:2016 certification and FDA registration for Class I and II devices", "Rapid prototyping via additive manufacturing, precision machining, and in-house PCB assembly", "FDA 510(k) documentation support with traceable design history files", "Flexible order volumes from low-volume prototypes to high-volume production"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Painesville, Ohio -> db", "FDA registration for Class I and II devices (Registration #) -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certifications -> /", "Formed from consolidation of Virtec Medical and Virtec Enterprises -> /", "End-to-end medical device development: concept, prototyping, validation, production -> /", "In-house capabilities: additive manufacturing, precision machining, injection molding, PCB assembly, custom cabling, tooling design -> /", "Volume range: prototype to medium-volume runs and high-volume production -> /", "Industries served: medical OEMs, startups, pilot programs -> /", "Specific applications: homecare dialysis, heated humidifiers, gastric calibration tubes, surgical tables, suction devices, laparoscopic devices, catheters, ventilatory devices, laser therapy, diagnostic devices, monitoring equipment, surgical devices, wearable/instrument-integrated designs -> /", "Vertically integrated U.S.-based model with single quality system -> /", "FDA 510(k) documentation support and traceable design history files -> /", "Rapid prototyping using additive manufacturing, precision machining, in-house PCB assembly -> /", "Flexible order volumes, low-volume production support -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DEM Medical is an FDA-registered manufacturer of Class I and Class II medical devices", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dem-medical-dba-virtec-enterprises' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DM Extrusion, doing business as DMC, operates from Spartanburg, South Carolina. The company manufactures extruded plastic sleeves and tubing for industrial and packaging applications, offering a range of diameters from 0.250 inch to 3.5 inches.

Materials processed include ABS, polypropylene, nylon, polyurethane, and polyethylene. Core capabilities encompass extrusion, custom grinding, forming, punching, surface-impregnated micro-grooving, anti-static treatment, molding, and shaping. The company also runs a recycling program for extruded plastic sleeves, allowing reclamation of production scrap and post-industrial material.

A key market is textile packaging, where the sleeves function as protective cores and packaging components. The product line further includes clear to black tubing for engineered molded and shaped applications serving broader industrial customers.

