UPDATE companies SET description='DMA Industries LLC is based in Tabor City, North Carolina, where it has established itself as a provider of private label programs for the automotive aftermarket.

The company delivers private label programs that define excellence in quality, speed-to-market, and value, supported by deep expertise in engineering, branding, packaging, logistics, and distribution. Its product lineup includes precision-engineered strut assemblies, installation kits with gaskets, fuel clips, and hardware, all meeting Grade 10.9 and SAE Grade 8 specifications. A strategic partnership with Zhejiang Sensen Auto Parts under the SDI joint venture added a manufacturing and distribution complex in Thailand, allowing DMA to avoid tariffs on Chinese-origin products while maintaining North American OE standards.

DMA serves automotive aftermarket distributors, retailers, and private label brands across North America. Its catalog spans makes from Acura to Volvo, and the company emphasizes direct customer service, promising that every call is answered by a knowledgeable person rather than an automated attendant.

The company says its integrated, end-to-end solutions and tariff-mitigation strategy set it apart, enabling faster speed-to-market and reliable supply for private label platforms.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Private label program development", "Engineering and design", "Branding and packaging", "Logistics and distribution", "Strut assembly manufacturing", "Precision casting", "Hardware kitting (gaskets, fuel clips, hardware)", "O.E. specification compliance", "Tariff mitigation via Thailand manufacturing", "Live phone customer support"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Private label programs"], "materials": ["Grade 10.9 steel", "SAE Grade 8 steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry-leading private label programs", "Deep expertise in engineering, branding, packaging, logistics, and distribution", "Fully integrated end-to-end solutions", "Manufacturing in Thailand avoids tariffs on China-origin products", "Direct customer service with no automated phone attendant"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Tabor City, North Carolina -> db", "Private label programs for automotive aftermarket -> db description", "Services: engineering, branding, packaging, logistics, distribution -> db description", "Products: strut assemblies, installation kits with gaskets, fuel clips, hardware -> db products", "Hardware specifications: Grade 10.9 and SAE Grade 8 -> db products", "Partnership with Zhejiang Sensen Auto Parts (SDI) -> /about", "Manufacturing and distribution complex in Thailand -> /about", "Tariff avoidance on China-origin products -> /about", "Customer service: no automated phone attendant, live person -> /about-us", "Product catalog covers many makes (Acura to Volvo) -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DMA Industries delivers industry-leading private label programs that define excellence in quality, speed-to-market, and value.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/dma-industries-llc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dma-industries-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DPS Molding, Inc. operates from Vanceboro, North Carolina.

The shop specializes in advanced injection molding techniques, including co-injection molding, co-injection with gas assist, structural foam molding, and rotary systems. It produces plastic components weighing up to 10 kilograms (22 pounds) and offers component design with gas assist, emphasizing thicker-walled, higher-value parts for demanding applications while promoting competitive costing and superior quality.

Its customer base spans the furniture, brush, and construction industries, where it supplies custom-molded plastic products.

The company distinguishes itself by focusing on recycling plastic through co-injection and structural foam processes, turning end-of-life products into new items—an approach it says regular injection molding cannot achieve. Its stated mission is to make products that last and then recycle them into new products, a philosophy it calls being "recycling artists."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Co-injection molding", "Co-injection molding with gas assist", "Structural foam molding", "Rotary systems", "Component design with gas assist"], "industries": ["Furniture", "Brush", "Construction"], "materials": ["Plastic", "Recycled plastic"], "equipment": ["Rotary systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Recycling plastic via co-injection and structural foam molding", "Designing thicker, higher-value parts for demanding markets", "Competitive costing and superior quality", "Parts up to 10 kg (22 lb)", "Component design with gas assist"], "facts_used": ["Location: Vanceboro, North Carolina -> db", "Industries: furniture, brush, construction -> db", "Processes: co-injection molding, co-injection with gas assist, structural foam molding, rotary systems -> homepage", "Part weight capacity: up to 10 kg (22 lb) -> db", "Recycling focus: co-injection and structural foam for recycling plastic -> homepage", "Component design with gas assist -> db", "Competitive costing and superior quality -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "focuses on manufacturing plastic products", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dps-molding-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DS Electronics, Inc. was founded in the early 1990s by Don Stemple in Tempe, Arizona. Now a second-generation family-owned and operated business, the company is headquartered in Gilbert, Arizona, where it manufactures electronic assemblies for customers worldwide.

The company provides full-service electronic contract manufacturing, including PCB assembly (surface-mount and through-hole), new product development, high-volume production, box-build and electro-mechanical assembly, test engineering, and supply-chain management. Its facility runs six independent SMT lines, multiple reflow ovens with custom thermal profiling validated by a KIC profiler, pick-and-place machines capable of 0201 and fine-pitch BGA placement, two robotic selective-solder cells, a wave-solder machine, and both 3D and 2D automated optical inspection systems. The operation supports prototype runs through high-volume commercial production.

DS Electronics serves industries such as LED lighting, semiconductor manufacturers, industrial electronics, and automotive. Customers range from early-stage design teams needing engineering support to established OEMs requiring large-scale, repeatable manufacturing.

