rizona -> db, /quality", "Six independent SMT lines -> /", "Multiple reflow ovens with custom thermal profiles -> /quality", "Pick and place machines for 0201 and BGA -> /quality", "Two 3D AOI machines and one 2D AOI machine -> /quality", "Two robotic selective solder machines and wave solder machine -> /quality", "KIC profiler for reflow validation -> /quality", "IPC-certified QC inspectors -> /quality", "Industries served: LED Lighting, Semiconductor Manufacturers, Industrial Electronics, Automotive -> /", "Services: PCB assembly, electronic contract manufacturing, new product development, high volume production, box build assembly, test engineering, supply chain, quality assurance -> /, /about-us", "Engineering-led management team: Don Stemple, Don Becker, Will Stemple, Andy Stemple -> /about-us", "Prototype to high-volume commercial production -> /about-us", "Locally manufactures in Gilbert, Arizona -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DS Electronics has been a leader in PCB assembly and electronic contract manufacturing services since the 1990s.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ds-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DSI Manufacturing was founded in 1982 in Rogers, Minnesota. The company operates as a precision sheet metal fabrication and CNC machining firm, led by President Joe Hines. From its inception, DSI has focused on building long-term customer partnerships through a structured process it calls the DSI Proven Process.

The company runs two facilities totaling more than 80,000 square feet, housing equipment for sheet metal fabrication — laser cutting, stamping, forming, welding, and in-house powder coating — as well as CNC milling (3-, 4-, and 5-axis), CNC turning and Swiss machining, and surface grinding. A dedicated Rapid Response Cell accelerates prototypes and short-run jobs, while collaborative design-for-manufacturability services help refine parts before production. DSI handles both quick-turn prototypes and high-volume production runs across metal and plastic materials.

DSI serves industries including retail fixtures and displays, machinery and equipment, electronics and computing, communications, automotive and recreational vehicles, oil and energy, agriculture, and fluid handling and filtration. Its customer base ranges from global retailers to technology firms seeking precision metal and plastic components.

