UPDATE companies SET description='Dana Poly Corp. was founded in 1990 in Dover, New Jersey, as a manufacturer of polyethylene film, bags, and sheet products. The company operates from a single New Jersey facility that has been producing plastic packaging in the United States since its inception.

The company’s core operations center on custom extrusion and converting of polyethylene resins into a wide range of products, including bin liners, box liners, drum liners, gaylord liners, pallet covers, furniture and mattress bags, anti-static bags, and construction sheeting. Its facility is strategically positioned adjacent to a dedicated rail stop that feeds resin directly into two large storage silos, and it features multiple loading bays for high-volume trailer shipments. Since 2017, the plant has been partially powered by a solar array, reflecting a stated commitment to reducing its carbon footprint.

Dana Poly serves industries such as packaging, textiles, furniture, construction, and specialized anti-static applications. Its customer base includes buyers of industrial liners, carpet and textile bags, furniture and mattress protection, and bed-bug barrier products, as well as general packaging purchasers seeking custom-printed film and sheeting.

The company emphasizes its HACCP and GMP certifications, an on-site quality control lab that conducts raw-material, in-process, and product-performance testing, and a resin development team that assists with material selection and design. Rail-direct logistics, solar energy, and high-speed printing presses are cited as factors that enable faster turnaround and cost efficiency.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','GMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom extrusion", "Converting", "Custom color blending", "Multi-color printing", "Process printing", "Consultation services", "Quality control testing (raw material, in-process, product performance)"], "industries": ["Packaging", "Textiles", "Furniture", "Construction", "Anti-static packaging", "Industrial liners"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Hexene"], "equipment": ["High-speed printing presses", "Large resin silos", "Railcar unloading system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Rail-direct resin delivery via dedicated rail stop", "Solar-powered facility since 2017", "HACCP and GMP certified manufacturing", "On-site quality control lab with specialized testing equipment", "High-speed printing presses for multi-color and process printing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990 in Dover, NJ -> db", "Manufacturer of polyethylene film, bags, sheet products -> /about-us", "Custom extrusion, converting, color blending, printing services -> /services", "Rail-direct logistics with dedicated rail stop and two large silos -> /", "Solar-powered since 2017 -> /", "HACCP and GMP certifications -> /, /about-us", "Quality control lab with raw material, in-process, product performance testing -> /quality", "Industries served: packaging, textiles, furniture, construction, anti-static -> /about-us", "Products: bin liners, box liners, drum liners, gaylord liners, pallet covers, furniture/mattress bags, anti-static bags, construction sheeting -> /about-us, /services", "High-speed printing presses -> /services", "Resin development and material selection expertise -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Dana Poly, Inc is a manufacturer of quality polyethylene film, bags, and sheet products.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dana-poly-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Danco Medical Systems, a family-owned business headquartered in Tipp City, Ohio, was founded in 1962 and has operated under family ownership since 1972. The company began by focusing on pharmacy and laboratory design, workflow optimization, and modular casework solutions for healthcare facilities.

Today, Danco provides a range of services including hospital pharmacy design, modular casework fabrication, IV hood selection and installation, USP 797/800 cleanroom configuration, and room sanitization systems. The firm also supplies a complete line of pharmacy cabinets, refrigerator/freezers, carts, and medication carousels from various manufacturers. Over its history, Danco has designed and equipped hundreds of facilities, supporting unit dose programs, pharmacy automation, and regulatory compliance.

The company serves hospital pharmacies, medical and dental offices, and laboratory environments. Its customers include institutions implementing USP Chapter 797 and 800 standards, adding automation to existing pharmacies, or building new cleanroom spaces.

