UPDATE companies SET description='DeKALB Molded Plastics operates from Butler, Indiana, where it has specialized in structural foam molding for more than 30 years. The company traces its roots to a founder and team committed to hard work and community involvement, though the founder’s name and exact founding year are not publicly disclosed.

The company focuses on large, multi-nozzle plastic components using structural foam injection molding and gas assist molding. Its press capacity spans 300 to 750 tons, supporting medium to large parts. In-house value-added operations include post-mold painting, plastic decorating, kitting, structural foam assembly, inventory management, fabrication, and labeling. Engineering support, advanced quality planning, statistical process control, and dimensional inspection round out the service offering.

DeKALB serves the structural plastics industry across diverse end markets. Named customers include Sauder Manufacturing, T.H.E.M. International, Signature Fencing & Flooring, PolyFlex Products Inc., EnerSys, Trinity, Fuji, Invivo, and Follett, which has sourced molded components since 2002.

