UPDATE companies SET description='Dickson Industries Inc. traces its roots to April 30, 1946, when Allied Manufacturing Co. was founded at 115 SW 8th Street in Des Moines, Iowa, to produce cotton stockinette for meat packers. Arthur D. Dickson, initially hired as a sales engineer, purchased the company in the 1960s, renamed it Dickson Industries, and moved operations to the Interstate Bakery Building at 325 SW 5th Street. The business remains a third‑generation, family‑owned enterprise; Arthur W. Dickson became president in 1972, and his son David Dickson assumed the role in 2014.

Today the company operates 216 high‑tech knitting machines and full cut‑and‑sew facilities across roughly 50,000 square feet, employing 49 people. Its product lines include custom knit fabrics, garments, and textile products: freezerwear and insulated apparel (Cold Room Coat, quilted vests), food‑processing nets and sleeves (DeliKnit, RoastKnit), industrial filtration covers (DrainKnit), and medical textiles such as PPE, lab coats, surgical drapes, and orthopedic fabrics. An in‑house embroidery division, Dickson Designs, adds custom branding.

Dickson serves food processors, medical and healthcare providers, industrial filtration OEMs, hospitality and footwear brands, and geotextile markets. Customers range from national meat‑packing plants to hospitals and international distributors, with the company’s centralized Midwest location enabling quick delivery across the United States.

The Dickson name emphasizes integrity, innovation, and a commitment to excellence backed by SQF certification (achieved in 2018) for food‑safety assurance. The company highlights confidential custom development, thorough testing, cost containment, and responsive service—including emergency shipping—as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Certification (Safe Quality Foods Institute)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom knitting", "Cut and sew operations", "Embroidery (Dickson Designs)", "Custom textile product design", "Filtration fabric manufacturing (DrainKnit)", "Medical textile manufacturing (PPE, lab coats, surgical drapes)", "Food processing garment manufacturing (DeliKnit, RoastKnit)", "Custom packaging and shipping", "Emergency response solutions", "Insulated apparel manufacturing", "Geotextile production", "Protective sleeve manufacturing"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Medical and healthcare", "Industrial filtration", "Hospitality", "Footwear", "Geotextiles", "Protective apparel", "Personal protective equipment (PPE)"], "materials": ["Cotton stockinette", "Yarn and fabrics", "Elastic netting (RoastKnit)", "Filtration media (DrainKnit)", "Medical-grade fabrics (surgical drapes, orthopedic fabrics)", "Insulated fabrics (freezerwear)", "Kapok (historical)"], "equipment": ["216 high-tech knitting machines", "Cut and sew equipment", "Embroidery machines (Dickson Designs)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SQF certification for food\u2011safety compliance", "216 knitting machines with integrated cut\u2011and\u2011sew operations", "Third\u2011generation family ownership ensuring continuity", "Custom product development with confidential specifications", "Midwest location for fast nationwide delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 as Allied Manufacturing Co. -> /about", "Headquarters Des Moines, Iowa -> db", "Employee count 49 -> db and /about", "Family-owned third generation -> /about", "SQF certification acquired 2018 -> /about and db certifications", "216 knitting machines -> /about", "Cut and sew operations -> /about", "Products: DeliKnit, RoastKnit, DrainKnit, medical textiles -> /about and /", "Industries: food processing, medical, industrial -> /about and /", "Custom embroidery (Dickson Designs) -> /about", "Centralized Midwest location for quick delivery -> /about", "Founder Arthur D. Dickson purchased company in 1960s -> /about", "Arthur W. Dickson became president 1972 -> /about", "David Dickson became president 2014 -> /about", "Facility ~50,000 sq ft -> /about", "SQF certification process started 2016 -> /about", "Expansion into Mexico 1965 -> /about", "Knitting operations in North Carolina and Tennessee 1980s -> /about", "DeliKnit business started 1998 -> /about", "Purchased 65 high-tech knitting machines 2005 -> /about", "Entered filtration industry 2000s -> /about", "In-house embroidery business 2017 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DICKSON INDUSTRIES, Inc. is a producer of quality, innovative knit fabrics, garments, and textile products for a multitude of target markets.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "49", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dickson-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DigitTron Technologies Inc. is an electronic component manufacturer based in Shawnee, Kansas, a suburb of Kansas City. The company was founded in 2011 and became a subsidiary of Pivot International in 2016, expanding its global reach with parent company offices in the UK, Hong Kong, and manufacturing facilities in Asia. Co-founder Victor Turnbaugh serves as general manager, a team that includes industrial designers, engineers, technicians, and assemblers.

The company operates a 13,800-square-foot, humidity-controlled facility where it provides surface-mount assembly, conventional through-hole assembly, X-ray inspection, box-build integration, potting, and conformal coating. Staff are trained to IPC workmanship standards, and the shop handles both small prototype runs and full production volumes without minimum order restrictions.

DigitTron serves customers in telecommunications, medical equipment, agriculture, transportation, lighting, and general industrial markets. Its client base spans hundreds of companies across the United States, ranging from start-ups to established OEMs.

The firm emphasizes a one-source model that combines design, assembly, and test under one roof, backed by rigorous quality control aligned with ANSI/J-STD-001, ANSI/J-STD-002, and IPC-A-610D standards. Management highlights cost management through smart design and on-time delivery as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI/J-STD-002','ANSI/J-STD-001','IPC-A-610D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface mount assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "Box build assembly", "X-ray inspection", "Potting", "Conformal coating"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Medical equipment", "Agriculture", "Transportation", "Lighting", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small to full production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One-source provider for surface-mount, X-ray, through-hole, and box-build assemblies", "13,800 sq. ft. humidity-controlled, clean facility", "Staff trained to IPC workmanship standards", "Quality control processes focused on cost management and on-time delivery", "Accepts small prototype runs through full production volumes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2011 -> db", "Headquarters Shawnee, Kansas -> db and homepage", "Subsidiary of Pivot International since 2016 -> /about-us", "Co-founder Victor Turnbaugh -> /about-us", "13,800 sq. ft. facility -> homepage", "Surface mount, through-hole, box-build, X-ray, potting, conformal coating -> homepage and capabilities", "Industries: telecommunications, medical, agriculture, transportation, lighting, industrial -> homepage and /about-us", "Certifications: ANSI/J-STD-002, ANSI/J-STD-001, IPC-A-610D -> homepage", "Staff trained to IPC workmanship standards -> homepage", "Quality control processes with cost management -> /quality", "Small and full production runs -> homepage", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are an electronic component manufacturing company headquartered in Shawnee, KS", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/382986/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='digittron-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Discount Moulding operates from its headquarters in Halethorpe, Maryland, and runs five showrooms across Chicago, Charlotte, Baltimore, Tysons Corner, and Charleston. The family-owned company was built on a volume-based model, purchasing moulding and interior doors by the truckload to keep prices low.

The company’s core service is in-house pre-hanging of doors, allowing customization of size, swing direction, jamb width, hinge color, and other specifications. It maintains a curated inventory of baseboards, casing, crown, shoe, flat stock, and interior doors, with most popular profiles available for next-day pickup or delivery from its showrooms.

Discount Moulding serves residential and light commercial builders, contractors, homeowners, and interior designers.

