UPDATE companies SET description='Dixon Power Systems is based in Lincoln, Nebraska. The company traces its roots to 1999 when Jon Dixon, after 17 years running an automotive repair shop, launched a part-time venture in renewable energy with encouragement from his wife Holly. The operation became full-time in January 2005.

The firm designs and installs custom solar photovoltaic and wind turbine systems for on-grid, off-grid, and backup-power applications. It also operates a storefront where customers can purchase pre-engineered system packages and components. No facility size or headcount figures are publicly disclosed.

Typical projects serve customers in remote locations without grid access, those pursuing environmental goals, and others wanting resilience against outages.

Jon Dixon’s background in automotive mechanical and electrical systems informed the company’s hands-on, problem-solving approach. He has pursued continuing education with industry experts and serves on the board of Nebraskans for Solar. The founders frame their mission around energy independence, emphasizing user-friendly designs that address each site’s unique constraints.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar PV system design", "Custom wind turbine system design", "Renewable energy system installation", "Off-grid and backup power system design", "Energy independence consulting", "Renewable energy equipment sales"], "industries": ["Residential renewable energy", "Commercial renewable energy", "Agricultural renewable energy", "Off-grid power", "Backup power systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom-designed systems tailored to each site\u2019s unique constraints", "Focus on energy independence and user-friendly operation", "Founder\u2019s hands-on mechanical and electrical expertise from automotive background", "Active involvement in renewable energy education and community advocacy"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 as part-time, full-time 2005 -> db", "Founders Jon and Holly Dixon -> db", "Location Lincoln, Nebraska -> db", "Jon Dixon automotive repair background -> /", "Design, installation, technical expertise -> /", "Storefront for system sales -> /", "Customer motivations: off-grid, backup, environmental -> /", "Jon Dixon education and board membership -> /", "Holly Dixon business management background -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "President / Design, Installation, Technical Expertise; opened a store-front where people could learn about and purchase systems to create their own electricity", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance":