UPDATE companies SET description='Drake Plastics Ltd. Co. operates from Cypress, Texas, where it was founded in March 1996 by Steve Quance. The company began when Quance, then an advanced products manager at a major stock-shape supplier, recognized that niche grades of Torlon® PAI were being neglected by large producers focused on high-volume output. A catalyst arrived when Atlantic Research Corporation needed glass-reinforced Torlon 5030 for the Javelin missile program and its existing supplier discontinued the product. Quance launched Drake to fill that gap, personally investing in specialized extrusion equipment and building a team around the technical demands of ultra high-performance polymers.

Today the company extrudes, injection molds, and precision machines a range of ultra high-performance polymers—including Torlon PAI, PEEK, Ryton R-4 PPS, AvaSpire PAEK, and Ultem PEI—into stock shapes, molded parts, and machined components. Its Cypress facility is described as the largest in the world dedicated to processing these materials, and it offers hybrid molded/machined solutions when tolerances exceed what molding alone can achieve. The operation also provides in-house CT inspection, CMM inspection, mechanical testing, re-curing, annealing, priming, coating, and laser engraving.

Drake serves aerospace and defense programs (notably the Javelin missile), OEMs, government agencies, universities, distributors, and fabricators worldwide. Sales offices in Germany, France, and Taiwan support global customers. The company’s stock shapes are supplied to machine shops globally, while its molded and machined parts go into applications such as electrical components, fluid handling, transportation, and oil and gas equipment.

The business was built on producing what larger suppliers could not or would not: niche grades in efficient sizes that minimize machining waste. Quance’s vision combined technical intuition with a commitment to long-term supply assurance, exemplified by the development of Drake 4200 PAI after Solvay discontinued Torlon 4200 resin. The company maintains AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 certification and reports on-time delivery of 98% or better.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion of ultra high-performance polymer stock shapes", "Injection molding of ultra high-performance polymers", "Precision plastic machining", "Hybrid molded/machined part production", "Product and process development", "CT inspection", "CMM part inspection", "Mechanical testing", "Material and process certification", "Re-curing and annealing", "Priming and coating", "Laser engraving", "Stock shapes for machining (rod, plate, tube, sheet, film, balls)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "OEMs", "Government agencies", "Universities", "Distributors", "Fabricators", "Oil and gas", "Transportation", "Electrical", "Fluid handling"], "materials": ["Torlon PAI (grades 4200, 4203, 5060, 5030, 7130, 4301, 4275, 4435, 4630, 4645)", "PEEK (grades KT820NT, 450 CA30, KT820CF30, KT820GF30, 450 FC30, 450FE20, HT)", "Ryton R4-240 PPS", "Ultem 2300 PEI", "AvaSpire PAEK (grades 621NT, 621GF30)", "Drake PAI (4200, Sheet/Film)", "CryoDyn CT-200", "Victrex HT"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Widest selection of stock shape sizes and configurations for ultra high-performance polymers", "Hybrid molded/machined part solutions for critical tolerances", "AS9100D/ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "On-time delivery typically 98% or better", "Largest facility in world dedicated to processing ultra high-performance polymers"], "facts_used": ["Founded March 1996 by Steve Quance in Cypress, Texas -> /ab