UPDATE companies SET description='Dynamic Packaging, LLC operates from Richmond, Virginia, where it designs and manufactures custom fabricated foam packaging solutions for shipping and transit applications. The company focuses on creating tailored protective packaging that addresses the specific physical characteristics of each client''s product.

The company provides complete turnkey services, from initial design consultation through final fabrication in its manufacturing facility. Its in-house capabilities include foam sawing and slicing, precision die cutting, CNC water jet cutting, and CNC heat bonding. The water jet cutting system requires no tooling investment, enabling fast prototyping and low-volume production. Dynamic Packaging also facilitates formal ISTA package drop and vibration testing when required. Its product range spans custom inserts for Pelican, Storm, and SKB cases, furniture leg protectors, end caps, foam enclosures, pocketed tray inserts, foam corners, box liners, anti-static packaging, ISPM15-compliant wooden crates, engineered pallets, and corrugated containers.

Dynamic Packaging serves manufacturers and shippers who need protective packaging for products transported in corrugated boxes, plastic or metal transit cases, wooden crates, and specialized hard cases. The company works with clients across various sectors that require reliable transit protection, though specific industry verticals are not publicly listed.

The company emphasizes lower set-up and tooling costs compared to molded Styrofoam, along with the ability to adjust designs quickly and inexpensively as products evolve. Its team identifies the appropriate foam type, density, and thickness for each application, and the in-house water jet cutting capability supports rapid iteration without tooling delays.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Foam sawing and slicing", "Precision die cutting", "CNC water jet cutting", "CNC heat bonding", "ISTA package drop and vibration testing facilitation", "Custom foam packaging design", "Prototyping", "Tooling and fabrication", "Custom case inserts (Pelican, Storm, SKB)", "Furniture leg protectors", "End caps and rails", "Foam enclosures", "Pocketed tray inserts", "Foam corners", "Foam box liners", "Anti-static packaging solutions", "Custom ISPM15 wooden crates and engineered pallets", "Corrugated containers"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Foam (multiple types)", "Anti-static foam", "Wood (ISPM15 compliant)", "Corrugated cardboard"], "equipment": ["CNC water jet cutting", "CNC heat bonding"], "volume": "Prototype and low-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lower set-up and tooling costs than molded Styrofoam", "Quick, inexpensive design changes as products evolve", "In-house CNC water jet cutting for fast prototyping and low-volume production", "Complete turnkey service from design consultation to final fabrication", "Facilitates formal ISTA drop and vibration testing"], "facts_used": ["Located in Richmond, Virginia -> db, /about", "Provides custom fabricated foam packaging -> /, /services", "Offers CNC water jet cutting and CNC heat bonding in-house -> /, /services", "Processes include foam sawing/slicing, precision die cutting -> /services", "Facilitates ISTA package drop and vibration testing -> /services", "Provides custom case inserts for Pelican, Storm, SKB cases -> /services", "Offers custom ISPM15 wooden crates and engineered pallets -> /services", "Design process includes consultation, CAD/solid model, prototyping, tooling, fabrication -> /services", "Benefits: lower set-up and tooling costs vs molded Styrofoam, quick design changes -> /", "In-house CNC water jet cutting for fast prototyping and low-volume production -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide complete turnkey services for all of your foam packaging needs. From initial design consultation to final approval, our team handles all aspects of the manufacturing for you.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dynamic-packaging-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Dynamic Sheetmetal Fabrication operates from St. Paul, Minnesota. The company was founded by Michael J. Herold, who brought 40 years of experience owning and operating precision sheet metal fabrication job shops. Herold serves as president and owner, a team whose senior members each have 30-plus years in the trade.

The shop specializes in precision sheet metal fabrication, offering laser cutting, turret punching, press brake forming, CNC machining, MIG/TIG welding, hardware insertion, deburring, finishing, and value-added assembly. Key equipment includes an Amada ENSIS 3015 AJ fiber laser with load automation, an Amada AE2510NT turret punch, two Amada press brakes (HG 8025 and HD 8025 NT), a Timesaver wet deburring machine, automated Haeger and Auto-Sert hardware insertion presses, a Scotchman cold saw, an Acer NC mill, a LeBlond lathe, and three Miller welding booths. The facility is climate-controlled and includes a cafeteria, locker rooms, and a 26-foot delivery truck for local shipments. Production runs from prototypes to full production, supported by SolidWorks design assistance and design-for-manufacturability reviews.

Dynamic serves high-tech markets and industrial clients. A testimonial from the president of a company developing industrial-sized hand sanitizer dispensers describes a partnership that spanned multiple prototype iterations through final production. The company''s leadership emphasizes experience across a multitude of high-tech sectors, though specific industry verticals are not listed publicly.

