ral Oregon rebate requirements -> /about", "Headquarters in Bend, Oregon -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Since 2005, E2 Solar has helped Central Oregon residents, businesses, builders, general contractors, nonprofits, and government agencies to generate smarter, cleaner power.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='e2-solar-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ECI Cables Inc. operates from a 50,000-square-foot facility in Sinking Spring, Pennsylvania. The company traces its roots to 1960, building over six decades of experience in cable and harness manufacturing. Since 2011 it has shared the modernized plant with its affiliate, RLC Electronic Systems, and completed a major expansion in 2021.

The shop specializes in custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, and equipment wiring, offering services that range from ribbon cable and DIN rail assembly to box builds, sensor assemblies, wire wrapping, and harness braiding. Four high-speed cutting and stripping machines handle wire from 0 to 30 AWG, while termination relies on multiple AMP presses, Pico pneumatic crimpers, and a large inventory of hand crimp tools calibrated to NIST standards. Cable identification capabilities include thermal transfer printing, hot stamping, and epoxy inking to meet military specifications. The facility also houses a Komax Alpha 530 and supports over-molding, crimp force monitoring, hi-pot, resistance, continuity, pull testing, and custom fixture validation.

ECI serves a broad industrial base that includes aerospace, automotive, agriculture, medical, data centers, renewable energy, transportation, water treatment, automation, fire safety, security, and lighting sectors.

